Signed off on **option 2**, with one correction from prod data.

Option 1 (add \`connection_id\` to the unique index) is now a live regression, not just a semantics change. In \`org_lobucrm\` today:

| namespace | distinct connections | rows |
|---|---|---|
| \`slack_channel_id\` | 3 | 9 |
| \`slack_user_id\` | 2 | 8 |

Those collisions are **correct** — the same Slack user seen through two connections should stay one person. A blanket index change splits that person into 2 entities and that channel into 3. So the prod data actively argues for the declared-property design rather than merely permitting it: whether an identifier means the same thing across connections is a property of the source system, and only the connector knows it.

Shape signed off:

